 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Check the reviews, both from regular customers and food blogs. Open table is a great way to see what the busy times are too. Some places post one or two on the website, but a quick search tells you more. A dish you've never heard of often means it' under the radar. It depends. Some places do one dish really well, and that's all they want to do. Others list everything they cook, so you can see the range. You' be much happier for it. And if the food turns out great, always order the most interesting looking dish, even if it' the one with the longest name.",
